---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="A Vision for Peterborough | AJ Shearer">
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-[#f8f1f3] text-[#3a1a22]">

    <!-- HERO -->
    <section class="bg-[#651024] px-6 py-16 text-white">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#f3dfe5] hover:underline"
        >
          ← Back to Main Site
        </a>

        <div class="mt-8 max-w-4xl">
          <div class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#f3dfe5]">
            A Vision for Peterborough
          </div>

          <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[#fff7f9] md:text-5xl">
            Better outcomes through practical, evidence-based decision making.
          </h1>

          <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-[#f3dfe5]">
            Peterborough's biggest challenges are connected. Affordability,
            homelessness, public safety, economic development, infrastructure,
            housing, and quality of life all influence one another.
          </p>

          <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-[#f3dfe5]">
            My approach is to understand those systems, recognize the incentives
            our decisions create, define the outcomes we actually want, and make
            the trade-offs necessary to move Peterborough in the right direction.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <main class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-20">

      <!-- INTRO -->
      <section class="rounded-3xl bg-white p-8 shadow-sm ring-1 ring-[#efe4e7] md:p-10">
        <div class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#651024]">
          Three Core Priorities
        </div>

        <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">
          What I'm focused on at City Hall
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          Throughout this campaign, and particularly through my
          <strong>Diary of a Transparent Candidate</strong> series, I've spent
          time speaking with residents, service providers, business owners,
          police, community leaders, and municipal stakeholders while digging
          into how Peterborough's systems actually work.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          Those conversations have sharpened my focus around three areas:
          protecting affordability through responsible government, building a
          stronger economic foundation for the city, and improving outcomes
          around homelessness and public safety.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          These aren't isolated issues. A stronger economy expands the tax base.
          A stronger tax base reduces pressure on homeowners. Better-performing
          social programs can improve outcomes for vulnerable residents while
          reducing pressure on emergency services and public spaces. Better
          infrastructure planning helps avoid larger costs in the future.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- AFFORDABILITY -->
      <section
        id="affordability"
        class="scroll-mt-24 mt-10 rounded-3xl bg-white p-8 shadow-sm ring-1 ring-[#efe4e7] md:p-10"
      >
        <div class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#651024]">
          Priority One
        </div>

        <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">
          Affordability & Responsible Government
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          The number one concern I continue to hear from residents is
          affordability. Families are dealing with higher mortgage payments,
          grocery bills, utilities, insurance, and property taxes. City Council
          can't control all of those pressures, but it does control how
          municipal dollars are spent and how quickly municipal costs grow.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          I don't believe responsible government means promising that taxes can
          simply be frozen regardless of circumstances. It means treating every
          dollar collected from residents as money that needs to produce value,
          carefully examining spending decisions, and keeping future increases
          as low as reasonably possible.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          That also means looking beyond the size of a budget and asking what
          we're actually getting for it. If a program is receiving more money,
          we should understand what outcome that investment is expected to
          produce and whether the evidence shows that it is working.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          Infrastructure is part of the same conversation. Roads, bridges,
          sidewalks, parks, public facilities, water, sewer, and stormwater
          systems become considerably more expensive when maintenance is
          deferred. Good asset management isn't flashy, but preventative
          maintenance and long-term planning can protect taxpayers from much
          larger bills later.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl bg-[#f8f1f3] p-6">
          <div class="text-lg font-bold text-[#651024]">
            My Focus
          </div>

          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-lg leading-7 text-[#7a6167]">
            <li>• Keep future property tax increases as low as reasonably possible</li>
            <li>• Review spending with a focus on measurable value and outcomes</li>
            <li>• Grow the commercial and industrial tax base</li>
            <li>• Reduce long-term pressure on residential taxpayers</li>
            <li>• Support preventative maintenance and long-term asset planning</li>
            <li>• Pursue partnerships and outside funding where they make financial sense</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ECONOMIC GROWTH -->
      <section
        id="prosperity"
        class="scroll-mt-24 mt-10 rounded-3xl bg-white p-8 shadow-sm ring-1 ring-[#efe4e7] md:p-10"
      >
        <div class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#651024]">
          Priority Two
        </div>

        <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">
          Economic Growth & Employment Lands
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          Peterborough cannot build long-term affordability simply by deciding
          how to divide up the tax burden. We also need to grow the economic
          base that supports the City.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          More private investment, commercial and industrial assessment, and
          good-paying jobs create opportunities for residents while also
          broadening the tax base that pays for municipal services and
          infrastructure.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          One of the biggest constraints facing Peterborough is the availability
          of employment land. The long-running discussion involving Peterborough,
          Cavan Monaghan, the County, and the Province represents an opportunity
          to think beyond municipal boundaries and pursue growth that can benefit
          the entire region.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          Many residents of surrounding communities already travel into
          Peterborough for jobs, shopping, healthcare, recreation, education,
          and other services. Likewise, Peterborough benefits from the workforce,
          businesses, land, and opportunities that exist around us. Our economies
          are interconnected whether our municipal boundaries acknowledge it or
          not.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          I believe the best path forward is collaborative rather than
          adversarial: work with Cavan Monaghan, the County, the Province,
          businesses, and landowners to create conditions where investment can
          happen and both communities can benefit.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          Economic development is also about the experience businesses have
          when they try to invest here. Serviced land, predictable rules,
          reasonable timelines, and certainty in the approval process are
          powerful incentives. Peterborough should continue looking for ways to
          make good investment easier without compromising appropriate planning
          standards.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl bg-[#f8f1f3] p-6">
          <div class="text-lg font-bold text-[#651024]">
            My Focus
          </div>

          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-lg leading-7 text-[#7a6167]">
            <li>• Move the employment lands discussion forward collaboratively</li>
            <li>• Work constructively with Cavan Monaghan, Peterborough County, and the Province</li>
            <li>• Increase the supply of serviced land available for employment growth</li>
            <li>• Attract private investment and good-paying jobs</li>
            <li>• Grow Peterborough's commercial and industrial assessment</li>
            <li>• Improve certainty and reasonable speed in development approvals</li>
            <li>• Support economic opportunities across sectors rather than relying on a single industry</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- PUBLIC SAFETY / HOMELESSNESS -->
      <section
        id="public-safety"
        class="scroll-mt-24 mt-10 rounded-3xl bg-white p-8 shadow-sm ring-1 ring-[#efe4e7] md:p-10"
      >
        <div class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#651024]">
          Priority Three
        </div>

        <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">
          Safer Streets & Better Outcomes
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          Homelessness, addiction, mental health, public disorder, and community
          safety are deeply interconnected issues. They also involve multiple
          levels of government, healthcare, police, social-service agencies,
          housing providers, community organizations, businesses, and residents.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          There is no single municipal program that can solve all of these
          problems. But that doesn't mean City Council is powerless. Council can
          be much clearer about the outcomes it expects from the services it
          funds and the partnerships it enters into.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          Compassion and accountability should not be treated as opposites.
          Helping someone remain trapped in homelessness or addiction is not the
          outcome we're looking for. The goal should be movement toward greater
          stability, appropriate treatment, housing, independence, and a safer
          community.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          That means asking better questions. How many people are entering a
          service? How many are moving into housing? How many are reconnecting
          with treatment or supports? How many return repeatedly? Are our
          interventions improving conditions in surrounding neighbourhoods and
          public spaces?
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          We also need to understand the incentives created by the systems we
          build. Well-intentioned policies can sometimes produce unintended
          consequences. Measuring those effects allows us to adjust programs
          rather than assuming that more activity automatically means better
          results.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          Public safety deserves the same evidence-based approach. Through this
          campaign I've had the opportunity to speak with police leadership,
          participate in a ride-along, and hear directly from downtown businesses
          and residents. Data can help identify where problems are occurring,
          which interventions are working, and where resources can have the
          greatest impact.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl bg-[#f8f1f3] p-6">
          <div class="text-lg font-bold text-[#651024]">
            My Focus
          </div>

          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-lg leading-7 text-[#7a6167]">
            <li>• Establish meaningful outcome measures for municipally funded homelessness programs</li>
            <li>• Focus on movement toward housing, treatment, stability, and independence</li>
            <li>• Examine the incentives and unintended consequences created by policy</li>
            <li>• Support evidence-based and data-driven policing</li>
            <li>• Protect residents, businesses, neighbourhoods, and public spaces</li>
            <li>• Improve coordination between the City, police, healthcare, service providers, and other levels of government</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- DECISION MAKING -->
      <section
        id="accountability"
        class="scroll-mt-24 mt-10 rounded-3xl bg-[#651024] p-8 text-white shadow-sm md:p-10"
      >
        <div class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#f3dfe5]">
          How I'll Make Decisions
        </div>

        <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">
          Understand the system. Measure the outcome.
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#f3dfe5]">
          One of the themes running through my entire campaign is that there are
          rarely perfect solutions in municipal government. There are trade-offs.
          Spending more in one area means that money isn't available somewhere
          else. A regulation intended to solve one problem may create another.
          A service designed to help people can sometimes create incentives that
          make the original problem harder to resolve.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#f3dfe5]">
          My professional background has taught me to start by understanding the
          system, defining the outcome we're actually trying to produce, and then
          using data and evidence to determine whether our decisions are moving
          us toward it.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#f3dfe5]">
          That doesn't mean every municipal decision can be reduced to a
          spreadsheet. Community values matter. Lived experience matters.
          Residents' priorities matter. But good information helps Council
          understand the consequences of the choices it is making and explain
          those choices honestly.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/10 p-6 ring-1 ring-white/15">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold">
              Understand the System
            </h3>

            <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-8 text-[#f3dfe5]">
              Look beyond the immediate symptom and understand how decisions
              affect the wider city.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/10 p-6 ring-1 ring-white/15">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold">
              Measure Outcomes
            </h3>

            <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-8 text-[#f3dfe5]">
              Judge programs by whether they are producing the results residents
              are paying for, not simply by activity or spending.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/10 p-6 ring-1 ring-white/15">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold">
              Understand Incentives
            </h3>

            <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-8 text-[#f3dfe5]">
              Consider how policies influence the behaviour of residents,
              businesses, organizations, and government itself.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white/10 p-6 ring-1 ring-white/15">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold">
              Be Clear About Trade-offs
            </h3>

            <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-8 text-[#f3dfe5]">
              Explain what residents gain from a decision, what it costs, and
              what alternatives Council considered.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 text-[#3a1a22]">
          <div class="font-bold text-[#651024]">
            Accountability also means communication
          </div>

          <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
            Residents should be able to understand what Council is deciding and
            why. I will work to communicate major issues in plain language,
            remain accessible to residents, listen carefully to different
            perspectives, and explain the reasoning behind the decisions I make.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- RECREATION / QUALITY OF LIFE -->
      <section
        id="recreation"
        class="scroll-mt-24 mt-10 rounded-3xl bg-white p-8 shadow-sm ring-1 ring-[#efe4e7] md:p-10"
      >
        <div class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#651024]">
          A City People Want to Live In
        </div>

        <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">
          Recreation, Arts & Quality of Life
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          A successful city is more than its tax rate or its balance sheet.
          Recreation, arts, culture, parks, sports, festivals, and community
          organizations help create the quality of life that makes people want
          to live, work, raise families, and invest in Peterborough.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          I've seen firsthand through my involvement with local sport and
          community organizations how much can be accomplished when residents,
          volunteers, businesses, non-profits, and government work together.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          I want Peterborough to continue investing in the things that make our
          city a great place to live, but I also believe new facilities and
          programs need to be evaluated against their full lifecycle costs and
          the value they provide.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-[#7a6167]">
          Partnerships can be an important part of that approach. Where
          community groups, private organizations, other governments, or outside
          funding can help provide amenities while reducing the burden on local
          taxpayers, those opportunities deserve serious consideration.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl bg-[#f8f1f3] p-6">
          <div class="text-lg font-bold text-[#651024]">
            My Focus
          </div>

          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-lg leading-7 text-[#7a6167]">
            <li>• Support recreation opportunities for residents of all ages</li>
            <li>• Support arts, culture, festivals, and community organizations</li>
            <li>• Encourage facilities that can serve multiple groups and activities</li>
            <li>• Explore public, private, and community partnerships</li>
            <li>• Consider lifecycle and operating costs before major investments</li>
            <li>• Use recreation and events to support tourism and local economic activity</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- DTC CONNECTION -->
      <section class="mt-10 rounded-3xl bg-[#2b0b14] p-8 text-white shadow-sm md:p-10">
        <div class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#f3dfe5]">
          Diary of a Transparent Candidate
        </div>

        <h2 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">
          See the thinking behind the platform.
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-[#f3dfe5]">
          These positions weren't developed in isolation. Throughout the
          campaign I've used my Diary of a Transparent Candidate series to share
          the meetings, research, questions, and experiences that are shaping
          how I think about Peterborough's challenges.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-[#f3dfe5]">
          The series explores housing and homelessness, public safety, economic
          development, infrastructure, data, incentives, and the trade-offs
          involved in municipal decision making.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
          <a
            href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLfzsxh8e8t4A"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="rounded-full bg-white px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-[#651024] shadow-lg"
          >
            Watch the Series
          </a>

          <a
            href="/"
            class="rounded-full border border-white/40 px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-white/10"
          >
            Return to Main Site
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

    </main>

    <!-- FOOTER -->
    <footer class="bg-[#651024] py-16 text-white">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
        <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-2 md:items-center">
          <div>
            <div class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#f3dfe5]">
              AJ Shearer
            </div>

            <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">
              Let's build a stronger Peterborough together.
            </h2>

            <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-[#f3dfe5]">
              If you'd like to learn more about my vision for Peterborough,
              volunteer, request a lawn sign, or simply share your thoughts,
              I'd love to hear from you.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 md:justify-end">
            <a
              href="/"
              class="rounded-full bg-white px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-[#651024] shadow-lg transition hover:-translate-y-0.5"
            >
              Main Website
            </a>

            <a
              href="https://www.facebook.com/VoteAJShearer"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="rounded-full border border-white/40 px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-white/10"
            >
              Facebook
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-12 border-t border-white/15 pt-6 text-sm text-[#f3dfe5]">
          © {new Date().getFullYear()} AJ Shearer • Candidate for Councillor,
          Monaghan Ward • City of Peterborough
        </div>
      </div>
    </footer>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>